WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.156 --> 00:00:18.438
Zann stuck the message moth in his pocket and then grabbed Zing.

2
00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:23.760
The little dragon had snatched a glowberry muffin away from one of the people watching the protest.

3
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.421
The man looked angry.

4
00:00:25.441 --> 00:00:29.322
"Zing!" Zann wrenched the muffin out of Zing's mouth.

5
00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:31.903
It had teeth marks and burns on it.

6
00:00:32.723 --> 00:00:33.784
Zann looked at the man.

7
00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:35.877
"I'll conjure you another one, sir."

8
00:00:35.897 --> 00:00:37.519
"You'd better!"

9
00:00:37.759 --> 00:00:38.479
the man grumbled.

10
00:00:38.499 --> 00:00:42.723
"There's a reason most people don't keep fire whistlers as pets, you know."

11
00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:47.387
Suddenly his expression changed and he peered closely at Zann.

12
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:51.090
"Wait, a fire whistler—hold on.

13
00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.152
Are you the Red kid who saved Magica from Morb?"

14
00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:58.235
Zann never knew what to say when people asked him questions like that.

15
00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:01.758
He couldn't have saved anything without help from his friends and others.

16
00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:03.720
So he said nothing.

17
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.283
Instead he rubbed his hands together to create a new glowberry muffin.

18
00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:10.144
But the man brushed it away.

19
00:01:10.164 --> 00:01:12.846
"I'm a reporter for the First City Flash.

20
00:01:13.566 --> 00:01:16.668
I came here to cover this protest, but nothing much is happening."

21
00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:21.051
With a snap of his fingers, he opened a note window in the air beside him.

22
00:01:21.732 --> 00:01:26.195
"I'd love to get your opinion on all the recent protests in First City," the reporter went on.

23
00:01:26.215 --> 00:01:31.178
"I'm sure everyone in Magica would love to know what their young Red hero thinks of the Void

24
00:01:31.218 --> 00:01:31.839
rights movement!"

25
00:01:32.539 --> 00:01:33.180
Zann shrugged.

26
00:01:34.072 --> 00:01:36.995
"I haven't been paying much attention," he answered truthfully.

27
00:01:37.015 --> 00:01:40.078
"I'm completely in favor of Void rights, of course.

28
00:01:40.738 --> 00:01:43.521
Other than that, I'm not very interested in politics."

29
00:01:44.181 --> 00:01:46.884
Zann's words appeared on the note window as he said them.

30
00:01:46.904 --> 00:01:49.666
"But you must have heard what people are saying."

31
00:01:50.347 --> 00:01:52.829
The reporter glanced at Zann's bright red hair.

32
00:01:52.849 --> 00:01:57.454
"Some non-Reds think the Red Council is almost as greedy as Morb himself.

33
00:01:58.114 --> 00:02:03.142
They say the Reds have too much power, and allowing them to control the relics Morb dug up

34
00:02:03.202 --> 00:02:03.903
is dangerous.

35
00:02:04.504 --> 00:02:09.548
They say that Magica's ancient relics belong to all citizens, and that the people should have a say

36
00:02:09.568 --> 00:02:10.489
in what happens to them.

37
00:02:11.029 --> 00:02:12.030
Not the Red Council."

38
00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:14.532
Zann had heard those comments.

39
00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:16.594
But he hadn't paid much attention to them.

40
00:02:17.214 --> 00:02:19.516
The relics were dangerous—that much he knew.

41
00:02:20.197 --> 00:02:23.560
They could have given Morb enough power to take over all of Magica.

42
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.244
But Zann trusted his parents and the others to handle the relics wisely now.

43
00:02:28.904 --> 00:02:32.065
"I'm sure my parents are doing what they think is best," he said.

44
00:02:32.086 --> 00:02:34.767
"But you’d have to ask them about the details."

45
00:02:35.927 --> 00:02:37.788
The reporter frowned at the note window.

46
00:02:38.428 --> 00:02:39.569
He seemed disappointed.

47
00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:41.990
Then he shrugged and brightened.

48
00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.331
"All right, then," the reporter said.

49
00:02:44.351 --> 00:02:46.852
"What's going on with you these days, Zann?

50
00:02:47.532 --> 00:02:52.975
I'm sure everyone would enjoy hearing an update on your life since Morb's, er, permanent departure."

51
00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:55.416
Zann winced at the last two words.

52
00:02:56.444 --> 00:02:59.625
Nobody ever came right out and said that Morb was dead.

53
00:03:00.266 --> 00:03:01.726
But Zann suspected he was.

54
00:03:02.387 --> 00:03:05.768
Wyssa had been furious when she'd dragged the villain through the vortex.

55
00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:13.331
But she'd never returned to Magica after that, so nobody knew for sure what she'd done with Morb.

56
00:03:13.351 --> 00:03:17.913
"I really need to go," Zann said, glancing toward his parents' lab.

57
00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:20.374
"This will only take a moment."

58
00:03:20.794 --> 00:03:21.915
The reporter smiled.

59
00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:24.456
"How are those friends of yours doing?

60
00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.521
I understand they returned to your old hometown."

61
00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:32.403
"Yes." Zann slid a hand into his pocket to check on the message moth.

62
00:03:32.423 --> 00:03:34.164
"We moved to First City.

63
00:03:34.444 --> 00:03:36.325
But their families are still in Swamp Bottom."

64
00:03:37.105 --> 00:03:38.366
"Yes, yes."

65
00:03:38.826 --> 00:03:43.188
The reporter glanced at the note window to make sure it was recording everything Zann said.

66
00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:49.090
"Speaking of family, I heard that your grandfather, Boz, came out of retirement to start working with the

67
00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.030
Red Council again.

68
00:03:50.631 --> 00:03:52.171
Is he helping to catalog the relics?"

69
00:03:52.911 --> 00:03:53.852
Zann bit his lip.

70
00:03:54.612 --> 00:03:57.353
"Um, I don't pay much attention to that kind of thing."

71
00:03:57.993 --> 00:04:00.695
He hoped the reporter would get bored and end the interview.

72
00:04:01.275 --> 00:04:03.356
But the reporter didn't look bored at all.

73
00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:06.137
"What was it like traveling through the vortex?"

74
00:04:06.437 --> 00:04:06.937
he asked.

75
00:04:07.597 --> 00:04:10.399
Zann hesitated, thinking back to those travels.

76
00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:13.360
Traveling through the vortex had been scary.

77
00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.321
It had also been exciting.

78
00:04:16.681 --> 00:04:19.082
But Zann didn't want to tell this stranger about that.

79
00:04:20.243 --> 00:04:23.144
He gulped and tried to think of some way to escape.

80
00:04:23.952 --> 00:04:24.652
"Excuse me!"

81
00:04:25.173 --> 00:04:27.174
A girl's voice came from behind Zann.

82
00:04:27.194 --> 00:04:30.575
"Are you a reporter for the First City Flash?"

83
00:04:31.275 --> 00:04:34.317
Turning, Zann saw a girl he recognized from school.

84
00:04:34.997 --> 00:04:37.618
She was a year ahead of him, and he didn't know her name.

85
00:04:37.638 --> 00:04:40.700
"Yes, I am," the reporter told her.

86
00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.040
"But I'm busy right now."

87
00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:44.041
"Okay," the girl said.

88
00:04:44.061 --> 00:04:47.083
"But I just heard that Laddno is here.

89
00:04:47.583 --> 00:04:49.564
He's speaking soon in the palace square."

90
00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.101
"Laddno is here?"

91
00:04:51.481 --> 00:04:52.682
someone nearby exclaimed.

92
00:04:52.702 --> 00:04:53.662
"Is that true?"

93
00:04:55.243 --> 00:04:55.943
The girl shrugged.

94
00:04:55.963 --> 00:04:56.744
"I don't know.

95
00:04:57.104 --> 00:04:57.964
It's just what I heard."

96
00:04:58.605 --> 00:04:59.785
The reporter looked excited.

97
00:04:59.805 --> 00:05:01.366
"I'd better get over there!"

98
00:05:01.566 --> 00:05:01.907
he said.

99
00:05:01.927 --> 00:05:03.367
"Thanks, young lady!"

100
00:05:04.488 --> 00:05:06.749
He snapped his fingers and zapped out of sight.

101
00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.690
Other people zapped away too.

102
00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.651
"Who's Laddno?"

103
00:05:10.991 --> 00:05:12.012
Zann asked the girl.

104
00:05:12.832 --> 00:05:13.393
She laughed.

105
00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.874
"I thought everybody had heard of him.

106
00:05:16.835 --> 00:05:18.976
He's a super-successful businessman.

107
00:05:19.648 --> 00:05:22.311
He's also the new leader of the Void rights movement."

108
00:05:22.931 --> 00:05:27.175
She rubbed her fingers together to conjure a dragon treat, which she tossed to Zing.

109
00:05:27.795 --> 00:05:31.399
The dragon snapped it up eagerly and then whistled happily at the girl.

110
00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:32.940
"Oh, right."

111
00:05:33.441 --> 00:05:36.143
Now Zann remembered hearing his parents mention the name.

112
00:05:36.764 --> 00:05:37.885
"Is Laddno a Void?"

113
00:05:37.905 --> 00:05:43.209
"No. He's just interested in equal rights for everyone in Magica.

114
00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:45.832
But listen, you should get out of here.

115
00:05:46.528 --> 00:05:50.950
That reporter might come back once he finds out Laddno isn't really speaking to the crowd."

116
00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:53.370
"Huh?" Zann was confused.

117
00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.652
"But you just said—" The girl giggled.

118
00:05:56.672 --> 00:06:02.574
"I could tell that you wanted the reporter to stop bothering you, so I said the one thing

119
00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:03.934
I knew would get him to leave."
